# Copy to your repository root as `.gitignore`.
#
# The first section is the one that matters. A secret committed and then
# deleted remains in history, in every clone, fork, and mirror, and in any CI
# cache. Deleting the file is not remediation — rotate the credential.

# --- Secrets and local configuration -------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
appsettings.Development.json
appsettings.Local.json
*.pem
*.key
*.pfx
*.p12
*.user

# --- Build output ---------------------------------------------------------
bin/
obj/
publish/
*.dll
*.pdb

# NOTE: packages.lock.json is NOT ignored. It must be committed — without it
# the same commit can resolve different dependency versions on different
# days, and `dotnet restore --locked-mode` in the pipeline will fail.

# --- Test and analysis output --------------------------------------------
TestResults/
coverage/
*.trx
*.coverage
coverage.opencover.xml
.sonarqube/
.scannerwork/
trivy-report.*
sbom-*.json
*.sarif

# --- Editor and OS --------------------------------------------------------
.vs/
.vscode/
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/settings.json
.idea/
.history/
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Local scratch --------------------------------------------------------
tmp/
temp/
*.local
*.log
